    systemPrompt:
        \\\
        We're working on the code located in ./src. Don't edit the spec located in ./spec.

        Before executing anything, read the spec it touches. Links to .claude/reference/... in the prompt are the spec for what they name. Read each one you need before changing anything it covers. Don't re-read something you've already read.

        Before changing anything, write the constraints this task must meet to ${UNDERSTANDING_FILE}, and keep it current as you read more of the spec. It is a Markdown list and nothing else: one line per constraint, at most twelve, each a single short, specific statement of what must be true, written as a link to the spec or reference file it comes from, such as `- [The chain tab has no bottom border in combined mode](spec/scope/prompt-mode/chat-input/index.pi)`. Only list what the spec says; leave out anything you are deciding yourself. Replace a constraint when you learn it was wrong rather than adding another.

        This prompt is the second step of a chain. Its first step changed the spec
        at ./spec to meet it, and the spec has been built since. Now change
        the code at ./src so it does what the spec now says, without
        changing the spec. Follow the spec the prompt references, and the anchors the
        spec step names below. Where the spec and the prompt disagree, follow the
        spec, and say so in your reply.

        The prompt the chain was sent:

        ${SPEC_PROMPT}

        What the spec step said it changed, its final output:

        ${SPEC_RESULT}
        \\\

    codeTask:
        prompt:
            \\\
            Let's revamp the @{BodyScope} to roughly match this styling
            \\\
        result:
            \\\
            I didn't change the spec this time, because your mockup's styling is already in it. The same request came in earlier this session, and the code was built to match then too. `piton check` finds no problems.

            **What the spec already says, matching the mockup:**
            - **In `BodyShape.description`** (`spec/scope/application/Body.pi`): the message list or open file sits on the flat #444444 base grey, edge to edge, with no line above the chat input.
            - **In `ChatInputShape`** (`spec/scope/prompt-mode/chat-input/index.pi`):
              - **Tab strip:** a flat 32px strip on #222222 with no lines anywhere. Each tab is just its coloured label with 8px either side. The selected tab is marked only by a #333333 background, joined to the input area below it.
              - **Input box:** #111111 with 4px corners and no border, 8px padding around it.
              - **Buttons:** a flat 88px column 8px apart. Send has a paper-plane icon, a semibold label and a muted slate colour (about #3b4252 for Spec). Queue and Preview are flat #444444.

            **Where the spec differs from the mockup, on purpose:**
            - **Tabs:** the mockup shows only Spec, Code, Ask and Agent. The spec keeps Code, Chain, Spec, Ask and Freeform, plus the help text and the right-hand controls (Slice, context, usage, New conversation). I read "roughly match this styling" as styling only. If you want the tab set changed, for example "Agent" replacing Freeform or Chain removed, tell me.
            - **Tab bar at the top:** the mockup has none above the message area. The spec keeps the Chat and file tabs there, since they're how open files are reached.
            - **Button heights:** in the mockup Send is slightly taller (~42px) than Queue and Preview (~35px). The spec makes all three the same height, matching the input's single row. Say if you want Send taller.

            **Anchors the code should follow:** `BodyShape.description`, `ChatInputShape.description`, and `ChatInputShape.tabs` (`overview`, `chain` and `colour`). The code in `src/chat_input.rs` already follows them, so the code step has nothing to change unless you decide on one of the differences above.

            The constraints are in `.suspense/history/1790754503-Prompt_98b144b88c058611.understanding.md`.
            \\\

    sentFrom: Prompt_98b144b88c058611
